# VII. Conclusion

** The study is worth studying, but is currently in the midst of the most significant changes in the pattern of competition in the company's history, requiring a high degree of analytical precision**

FICO is a very good company in the past: 82% Māori, 47% EBIT, 37% Free Cash Flow Profit, and multi-year double-digit growth. Morning Stars give fair value of $2,020 (71% higher than current prices) to reflect recognition of its core competitiveness.

But the pattern of competition changed qualitatively in 2026. VantageScore was recognized by GSE, credit authorities promoted alternatives at a price of 1/10, and DOJ launched antimonopoly investigations – three of which occurred simultaneously, exposing FICO to the most serious competition challenge in 70 years of existence.

** Core judgement point: ** How much share FIO can hold in the mortgage rating market? If 70% + is saved, the current stock price is indeed seriously underestimated; if the share falls below 50% and the price is forced to drop significantly, the target price of $2,020 will be unrealistic.

The suggested focus studies: (1) progress in the actual adoption of VantageScore among lenders (not approved progress, but actual use of data); (2) whether FICO has started to reduce prices to respond; and (3) whether the Q3/Q4 SY2026 rating income growth has been reversed.

